# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Note:** CPU time is the post-processing time. The three mirror circuits were submitted together in one run, so the recorded QPU and CPU times are for all three circuits together. Each Clifford circuit run contained nine PUBs with different circuit depths, so the recorded times are for all nine PUBs together. Each Ising circuit run contained 10 PUBs with different numbers of Trotter steps, so the recorded times are for all 10 PUBs together.\n"
msgstr "**Nota:** el tiempo de CPU es el tiempo de posprocesamiento. Los tres circuitos espejo se enviaron juntos en una sola ejecución, por lo que los tiempos de QPU y CPU registrados corresponden a los tres circuitos en conjunto. Cada ejecución de circuito de Clifford contenía nueve PUB con distintas profundidades de circuito, por lo que los tiempos registrados corresponden a los nueve PUB en conjunto. Cada ejecución de circuito de Ising contenía 10 PUB con distinto número de pasos de Trotter, por lo que los tiempos registrados corresponden a los 10 PUB en conjunto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the mirror circuits, the benchmarks use the RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal, and EfficientSU2 ansätze with 30, 35, and 40 qubits, respectively. The observables consist of a single Pauli-$Z$ operator on a randomly selected qubit, with an ideal expectation value of 1.\n"
msgstr "Para los circuitos espejo, los benchmarks usan los ansätze RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal y EfficientSU2 con 30, 35 y 40 qubits, respectivamente. Los observables consisten en un único operador de Pauli-$Z$ sobre un qubit seleccionado al azar, con un valor esperado ideal de 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the Clifford circuits, the benchmarks use 50- and 100-qubit circuits with observables initialized as one or more randomly positioned Pauli-$Z$ operators. Operator evolution increases the Pauli weight of these observables, which provides more complex observables for benchmarking. The observables are constructed to have an ideal expectation value of 1, which is independently verified with stabilizer simulation.\n"
msgstr "Para los circuitos de Clifford, los benchmarks usan circuitos de 50 y 100 qubits con observables inicializados como uno o más operadores de Pauli-$Z$ en posiciones aleatorias. La evolución del operador aumenta el peso de Pauli de estos observables, lo que proporciona observables más complejos para el benchmarking. Los observables se construyen para tener un valor esperado ideal de 1, que se verifica de forma independiente con simulación de estabilizadores.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the Trotterized 2D tilted-field Ising (TFI) Hamiltonian simulations, the benchmarks use three parameter regimes: small angle $(\\theta_X,\\theta_Z,\\theta_{ZZ})=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, near-Clifford $(0.1,0.05,1.5708)$, and chaotic $(0.53,0.1,1.0)$. The observable is the average magnetization,\n"
msgstr "Para las simulaciones del hamiltoniano de Ising de campo inclinado 2D (TFI) con Trotterización, los benchmarks usan tres regímenes de parámetros: ángulo pequeño $(\\theta_X,\\theta_Z,\\theta_{ZZ})=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, casi de Clifford $(0.1,0.05,1.5708)$ y caótico $(0.53,0.1,1.0)$. El observable es la magnetización promedio,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O_M = \\frac{1}{M}\\sum_i Z_i,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O_M = \\frac{1}{M}\\sum_i Z_i,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $M$ is the number of qubits in the simulation. Ideal expectation values are computed with sparse Pauli dynamics (SPD), a Pauli propagation method, and are validated against Qiskit statevector simulations for circuits with fewer than 29 qubits.\n"
msgstr "donde $M$ es el número de qubits de la simulación. Los valores esperados ideales se calculan con dinámica de Pauli dispersa (SPD), un método de propagación de Pauli, y se validan con simulaciones de statevector de Qiskit para circuitos con menos de 29 qubits.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For all benchmarks, mitigation accuracy is calculated as\n"
msgstr "Para todos los benchmarks, la precisión de la mitigación se calcula como\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Accuracy}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Accuracy}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\left(\n"
"1-\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\left|\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}-\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}\\right|\n"
"}{\n"
"\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}\n"
"}\n"
"\\right)\\times100\\%,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\left(\n"
"1-\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\left|\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}-\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}\\right|\n"
"}{\n"
"\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}\n"
"}\n"
"\\right)\\times100\\%,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}$ and $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}$ are the ideal and mitigated expectation values, respectively.\n"
msgstr "donde $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}$ y $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}$ son los valores esperados ideal y mitigado, respectivamente.\n"

